RangeForce: Windows Local Privilege Escalation Techniques

Platform: RangeForce  
Room: Windows Local Privilege Escalation Techniques  
Difficulty: Advanced  
Date: 2026  

Objective  
The objective of this lab was to identify and exploit common Windows local privilege escalation techniques to gain elevated access on a compromised system.

Tools & Techniques Used  
- Plaintext credential discovery  
- AlwaysInstallElevated misconfiguration  
- Unquoted service path exploitation  

Methodology  

1. Plaintext Credentials  
Identified plaintext credentials stored on the system and used them to escalate privileges.

2. AlwaysInstallElevated  
Exploited the AlwaysInstallElevated policy misconfiguration to execute a malicious MSI file with elevated privileges.

3. Unquoted Service Path  
Identified a vulnerable unquoted service path and placed a malicious executable in the path to achieve privilege escalation when the service was executed.

Key Findings  
- Storing credentials in plaintext introduces significant security risk.  
- Misconfigured policies like AlwaysInstallElevated can be easily abused for privilege escalation.  
- Unquoted service paths provide a reliable method for escalating privileges.  

Conclusion  
This lab demonstrated multiple Windows privilege escalation techniques, highlighting the importance of secure configurations, proper credential management, and system hardening to prevent unauthorized elevation of privileges.
